cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "Please cite this software repository when using its code or saved numerical tables. The associated manuscript is currently unpublished."
title: "Retinal Vessel Flow Refinement with OOF Inputs"
authors:
  - family-names: Bayanian
    given-names: Babak
  - family-names: Naderi
    given-names: Hanieh
  - family-names: Dinesh
    given-names: Chinthaka
date-released: "2026-11-19"
url: "https://github.com/thebabak/retinal-vessel-flow-refinement-oof"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thebabak/retinal-vessel-flow-refinement-oof"
abstract: >-
  Research code, manuscript and saved verified tables for the three-dataset
  study of Flow Matching and matched Direct retinal-vessel refinement using
  native patches and nested out-of-fold inputs. Five correction-training seeds
  are conditional on shared upstream fits. Calibrated corrections improve
  some endpoints, but a Flow-specific advantage is not established. The
  associated manuscript is unpublished and has no asserted manuscript DOI.
keywords:
  - retinal vessel segmentation
  - flow matching
  - out-of-fold predictions
  - native-resolution patches
  - reproducibility
